#: packaging/data/io.winspace.Development.Native.desktop packaging/data/io.winspace.Development.Native.metainfo.xml packaging/data/io.winspace.Development.desktop packaging/data/io.winspace.Development.metainfo.xml
msgid "File Explorer"
msgstr ""

#: packaging/data/io.winspace.Development.Native.desktop packaging/data/io.winspace.Development.desktop
msgid "File Explorer;file explorer;File Manager;files;folders;SMB;NAS;network;archives;"
msgstr ""

#: packaging/data/io.winspace.Development.Native.desktop packaging/data/io.winspace.Development.Native.metainfo.xml
msgid "OpenXplorer Native Preview"
msgstr ""

#: packaging/data/io.winspace.Development.Native.desktop packaging/data/io.winspace.Development.Native.metainfo.xml
msgid "Preview of the native OpenXplorer file manager"
msgstr ""

#: packaging/data/io.winspace.Development.Native.metainfo.xml packaging/data/io.winspace.Development.metainfo.xml
msgid "A name being renamed in place no longer closes when you use its own right-click menu, such as Paste or Select All, or switch to another window. Item check boxes are off by default, so a selected item is only highlighted, as in Windows; View > Item check boxes turns them back on. A search word found only in a name's extension no longer matches, so pd no longer finds every PDF."
msgstr ""

#: packaging/data/io.winspace.Development.Native.metainfo.xml packaging/data/io.winspace.Development.metainfo.xml
msgid "A notice at the top right of the window says when a new release is out, the command bar's Update and the status bar's Update available stay until it is installed, and the Settings gear is back in the command bar. Deleting a folder permanently under Open as administrator works again for folders 2.0.12 and 2.0.13 refused, through a small helper that holds each folder open while it empties it. Dragging a tab out into a new window no longer crashes on Wayland, and the keyboard returns to the file list after navigating or editing the address."
msgstr ""

#: packaging/data/io.winspace.Development.Native.metainfo.xml
msgid "A preview of the next OpenXplorer, drawn with native GTK 4 widgets instead of a web page. It browses local folders, SMB shares and connected phones in the familiar tabbed window styled after Windows 11 File Explorer."
msgstr ""

#: packaging/data/io.winspace.Development.Native.metainfo.xml packaging/data/io.winspace.Development.metainfo.xml
msgid "Adds Windows Explorer's Group by, separate from the sort, and Folder Options' Apply to all folders and Reset folders. Copies ask about one unreadable file instead of failing the folder and about names Windows cannot use, TAR archives get the ZIP safety limits, read-only and disconnected drives say so, and the Open and Save dialogs no longer freeze or get stuck."
msgstr ""

#: packaging/data/io.winspace.Development.Native.metainfo.xml packaging/data/io.winspace.Development.metainfo.xml
msgid "Adds a Simplified Chinese translation, used when the desktop's language is Chinese; every other language, and a desktop that lists English first, stays in English. Recent files and the other sidebar rows, the Open with and Terminal menu entries, folder sizes and the About page are now translatable too."
msgstr ""

#: packaging/data/io.winspace.Development.Native.metainfo.xml packaging/data/io.winspace.Development.metainfo.xml
msgid "Adds item check boxes as in Windows 11 and a redesigned Settings page with eight pages, a search across all of them and details in ⓘ bubbles. Open and Save dialogs no longer wait on network shares and say why Save cannot save, and a folder's expand arrow stays inside its row's highlight. Dropping files onto a file on a Windows drive or share no longer runs it unless it really is a program, and asks first."
msgstr ""

#: packaging/data/io.winspace.Development.Native.metainfo.xml packaging/data/io.winspace.Development.metainfo.xml
msgid "Brave's downloads, its Save page as and Save as PDF, and its upload dialogs can open OpenXplorer's own Open and Save dialogs, also when the desktop portal reads its settings from a different folder, and the Brave sync can make Brave ask where to save each download. A Save dialog names the file for the type chosen in it. By default, an unselected item's check box shows on hover only while Ctrl is held, as in Windows Explorer, and an experimental, off-by-default option indexes frequently opened folders for instant search. Compressed archives, launcher previews during a drag and search results now have memory limits, and the share mount helper only rolls back what its own setup changed. Large cached folders, fast file operations and custom folder icons take less time."
msgstr ""

#: packaging/data/io.winspace.Development.Native.metainfo.xml packaging/data/io.winspace.Development.metainfo.xml
msgid "Copies, drags and new folders work as in Windows Explorer: a copy is named “name - Copy”, a plain drag moves within a drive and copies to another, and New folder makes the folder at once to rename in place. Properties shows Size on disk, a rename that changes the extension asks first, and Super+E can open OpenXplorer on KDE Plasma. An empty folder looks as it does in Windows and takes right-click, paste and drops, New and Paste are off in a folder you cannot write to, Apply to all folders uses the choices in the dialog, and Show after moving items to the Recycle Bin opens it."
msgstr ""

#: packaging/data/io.winspace.Development.Native.metainfo.xml packaging/data/io.winspace.Development.metainfo.xml
msgid "Deleting a folder permanently under Open as administrator is now also refused on drives an ordinary user can mount or plug in: drives that /etc/fstab lets users mount, drives a user mounted, and removable, USB, SD card, FireWire, Thunderbolt and loop devices."
msgstr ""

#: packaging/data/io.winspace.Development.Native.metainfo.xml packaging/data/io.winspace.Development.metainfo.xml
msgid "File Manager"
msgstr ""

#: packaging/data/io.winspace.Development.Native.metainfo.xml
msgid "First packaged native preview of the GTK 4 interface, for trying it beside the current OpenXplorer."
msgstr ""

#: packaging/data/io.winspace.Development.Native.metainfo.xml packaging/data/io.winspace.Development.metainfo.xml
msgid "Folder Options replaces Adjust view display style, with Windows' General and View tabs, and Windows Explorer's Ctrl+E, Ctrl+D, F11 and Alt+P work. The Share button emails the selected files through the desktop's email app. Delete moves items to the Recycle Bin wherever it works and asks only about items that cannot go there. As in Windows Explorer, a file operation that succeeds or is cancelled says nothing and sends no desktop notification, while failures, and failures not yet shown when you cancel, are still reported; read-only drives are not singled out, and New and Paste stay on in folders you cannot write to; Undo stays on Ctrl+Z and the folder menu. Keys meant for an open dialog no longer reach the files behind it, menus show in full when they fit on the monitor, submenus open in the same popup, a cut item pasted into its own folder stays put, and a failed copy names the real file."
msgstr ""

#: packaging/data/io.winspace.Development.Native.metainfo.xml packaging/data/io.winspace.Development.metainfo.xml
msgid "Make OpenXplorer default also sends other apps' Open and Save dialogs to OpenXplorer, and GTK 3 apps use them too after the next login. Format on a removable drive opens OpenXplorer's own Format dialog instead of GNOME Disks, and Enter in Extract all extracts. Deleting many files on a share asks the server about each file once instead of three times. A move between drives keeps the source files of a folder it skipped partway, Undo asks first when it cannot check a whole copy, signing out of a server forgets its passwords on every port, and the Recycle Bin and search results no longer show stale items."
msgstr ""

#: packaging/data/io.winspace.Development.Native.metainfo.xml packaging/data/io.winspace.Development.metainfo.xml
msgid "NAS"
msgstr ""

#: packaging/data/io.winspace.Development.Native.metainfo.xml packaging/data/io.winspace.Development.metainfo.xml
msgid "OpenXplorer contributors"
msgstr ""

#: packaging/data/io.winspace.Development.Native.metainfo.xml
msgid "Preview build of OpenXplorer 2.0.0 under its own application ID."
msgstr ""

#: packaging/data/io.winspace.Development.Native.metainfo.xml
msgid "Preview build of OpenXplorer 2.0.1 under its own application ID."
msgstr ""

#: packaging/data/io.winspace.Development.Native.metainfo.xml
msgid "Preview build of OpenXplorer 2.0.2 under its own application ID."
msgstr ""

#: packaging/data/io.winspace.Development.Native.metainfo.xml packaging/data/io.winspace.Development.metainfo.xml
msgid "Running copies, moves and deletes show in a Windows-style progress window, and Properties is redone as Windows 11's Properties windows. Several selected items can be renamed at once, a new text document is created at once and renamed in place, tabs drag as in Chrome, and the menus and defaults match Windows 11 Explorer. A slow location shows at once that it is opening, search is faster and more reliable, and Copy as path quotes each path. Deleting a folder permanently under Open as administrator is refused when other accounts can change it, and a share another app asks OpenXplorer to show is connected to only when you choose Try again."
msgstr ""

#: packaging/data/io.winspace.Development.Native.metainfo.xml packaging/data/io.winspace.Development.metainfo.xml
msgid "SMB"
msgstr ""

#: packaging/data/io.winspace.Development.Native.metainfo.xml packaging/data/io.winspace.Development.metainfo.xml
msgid "Search results no longer refresh every few seconds while folders are being indexed, so a result you select stays selected. A search of a folder nobody indexed no longer starts over, and a cached search updates in place instead of showing Searching again."
msgstr ""

#: packaging/data/io.winspace.Development.Native.metainfo.xml
msgid "The preview is incomplete and runs beside the current OpenXplorer without replacing it. It never changes file associations, browser preferences or network mounts."
msgstr ""

